<% content_for :title, "Review workflow · Kode Stack Demos" %>

<header class="mb-6">
  <h1 class="page-title">Review workflow</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-slate-600">
    A coded chart moves from draft to review, then back to the coder or on to approval, and it can only move along
    those paths: an <code>aasm</code> state machine refuses anything else, and PaperTrail records who changed what and
    when, down to the field. That pairing is how a QA workflow stays honest, because nobody can skip review or
    quietly edit a code without it showing up in the audit trail. Act as the coder or the reviewer from the switch
    below; the reviewer edits codes inline and can press <kbd>a</kbd> to approve or <kbd>r</kbd> to return.
    The codes are real ICD-10-CM codes; every chart is synthetic.
  </p>
</header>

<%= render "review/shared/toolbar" %>
<%= render "review/shared/flash" %>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <% @groups.each do |state, charts| %>
    <section aria-labelledby="state-<%= state %>">
      <h2 id="state-<%= state %>" class="mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span class="section-label"><%= Review::Chart::STATE_LABELS.fetch(state) %></span>
        <span class="<%= Review::Chart::STATE_BADGES.fetch(state) %>" aria-label="<%= pluralize(@counts.fetch(state, 0), "chart") %>"><%= @counts.fetch(state, 0) %></span>
      </h2>
      <% if charts.any? %>
        <ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <% charts.each do |chart| %>
            <li>
              <%= link_to review_chart_path(chart), class: "card-link", id: dom_id(chart) do %>
                <p class="font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= chart.title %></p>
                <p class="mt-1 line-clamp-2 text-sm text-slate-600"><%= chart.encounter_summary %></p>
                <p class="mt-3 text-xs font-medium text-slate-500"><%= pluralize(chart.codes.size, "code") %></p>
              <% end %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-500">No charts.</p>
      <% end %>
    </section>
  <% end %>
</div>
